A||||5||GT Bastard||What valve springs did you use with your Compucam?||||5||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||02-09-2001||06:43 PM||||Just curious if people are using factory springs with their Crane Compucam or going with stiffer ones.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||lou_dias||02-09-2001||07:16 PM||||I used the crane "double" springs.  Don't recall the part number but they are in the crane catalog and the Fiero Store has them too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||02-09-2001||07:48 PM||||GT Bastard you should get he recommended springs and retainers for your Crane camshaft. The factory springs are only suitable for .420” maximum valve lift according to GM and the Crane Compucam has .423.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||02-10-2001||08:21 AM||||I hope I can get them in the next couple days... I've gotta get this GT together, and I wanna use that cam.  I doubt the local auto part stores will have them...  Do machine shops typically carry different types of springs?  <P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hartz||02-10-2001||09:08 AM||||When I did my Compucam, I used the Compucam lifters, and Crane valve springs (p/n 99848-12), retainers (p/n 99915-12), and locks (p/n 99041-1).<P>Best of luck,<P>Hartz<BR>'85 SE V6 Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phaeton||02-10-2001||12:20 PM||||Using the compucam with aluminum heads tapped for small block studs and using ZZ3 springs.  They fit right in and have more seat pressure for the amount of work required than the dual springs I checked out.  But I like to mix and match parts just to be different.  Sometimes I get bit in the ace later but it's always an adventure.||||reg||12
